/*
 * ============================================================================
 * ESP32 Control ESP-NOW - Wireless Controller with Franzininho WiFi (ESP32-S2)
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * This sketch implements a wireless remote controller using ESP-NOW protocol.
 * It communicates with a robot receiver to control movement with variable speed.
 * Displays real-time status on an OLED screen including signal strength (RSSI)
 * and connection state.
 *
 * HARDWARE:
 * - Franzininho WiFi (ESP32-S2)
 * - 6 buttons (directional pad + speed control)
 * - SSD1306 OLED display (128x64) connected via I2C
 *
 * BUTTON MAPPING:
 * - UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT: Movement control
 * - Button A: Increase speed
 * - Button B: Decrease speed
 *
 * COMMUNICATION:
 * - Protocol: ESP-NOW (peer-to-peer WiFi)
 * - Reliability: Automatic retransmission with ESPNowProtocol library
 * - Message Types: Control commands and telemetry reception
 * - Auto-discovery: Enabled for automatic peer detection
 *
 * DEPENDENCIES:
 * - ESPNowProtocol (GitHub: https://github.com/FBSeletronica/ESPNowProtocol)
 * - Adafruit_SSD1306 (OLED display driver)
 * - Adafruit_GFX (Graphics library)
 * - Adafruit_BusIO (I2C/SPI abstraction)
 *
 * AUTHOR: Fabio Souza
 * LICENSE: MIT License
 * VERSION: 1.2
 * 
 * ============================================================================
 */

